\begin{abstract}
  Based on work of Alain Connes, I have constructed a spectral interpretation
  for zeros of $L$-functions.  Here we specialise this construction to the
  Riemann $\zeta$-function.  We construct an operator on a nuclear Fréchet
  space whose spectrum is the set of non-trivial zeros of~$\zeta$.  We exhibit
  the explicit formula for the zeros of the Riemann $\zeta$-function as a
  character formula.
\end{abstract}

